52618	52629	52631	52631	Mary	138	" But how was your daughter when you got there ? "
52635	52749	51772	51779	the last to jar on the full heart	1859	" She were at rest , poor wench , and so were Frank . I guessed as much when I see'd th ' landlady 's face , all swelled wi ' crying , when she opened th ' door to us . We said , ' Where are they ? ' and I knew they were dead , fra ' her look ; but Jennings did n't , as I take it ; for when she showed us into a room wi ' a white sheet on th ' bed , and underneath it , plain to be seen , two still figures , he screeched out as if he 'd been a woman .
52750	52813	51772	51779	the last to jar on the full heart	1859	" Yet he 'd other childer and I 'd none . There lay my darling , my only one . She were dead , and there were no one to love me , no , not one . I disremember [ 31 ] rightly what I did ; but I know I were very quiet , while my heart were crushed within me .
52818	52821	51772	51779	the last to jar on the full heart	1859	" Disremember , "
